e>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":8},{"id":"ed26d3d8","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## 7. Federated simulation\n\nThe FL clients are **controlled partitions of the training records**. In the manuscript, call them **simulated clients / decentralized data partitions**, not identified classrooms or students.\n\nPartition modes:\n\n- **IID:** approximately balanced label composition.\n- **Dirichlet label skew:** controlled changes in `P(y | client)`.\n- **Feature-cluster skew:** controlled differences in feature composition; explicitly described as a simulation, not a reproduction of real device populations.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"1ab4370b","cell_type":"code","source":"\n# 7A. Partition helpers\ndef balanced_iid_partition(y, n_clients, seed):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    parts = [[] for _ in range(n_clients)]\n    for cls in np.unique(y):\n        idx = rng.permutation(np.where(y == cls)[0])\n        for k, s in enumerate(np.array_split(idx, n_clients)):\n            parts[k].extend(s.tolist())\n    return [np.array(sorted(z), dtype=int) for z in parts]\n\ndef dirichlet_label_partition(\n    y,\n    n_clients,\n    alpha,\n    seed,\n    min_size=100,\n    max_tries=500\n):\n\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    classes = np.unique(y)\n\n    for attempt in range(1, max_tries + 1):\n\n        parts = [[] for _ in range(n_clients)]\n\n        for cls in classes:\n\n            idx = rng.permutation(\n                np.where(y == cls)[0]\n            )\n\n            props = rng.dirichlet(\n                np.ones(n_clients) * alpha\n            )\n\n            cuts = (\n                np.cumsum(props) * len(idx)\n            ).astype(int)[:-1]\n\n            splits = np.split(idx, cuts)\n\n            for k, s in enumerate(splits):\n                parts[k].extend(\n                    s.tolist()\n                )\n\n        sizes = [\n            len(z)\n            for z in parts\n        ]\n\n        if min(sizes) >= min_size:\n\n            return [\n                np.array(\n                    sorted(z),\n                    dtype=int\n                )\n                for z in parts\n            ]\n\n    raise RuntimeError(\n        f\"Could not build Dirichlet partition after \"\n        f\"{max_tries} attempts \"\n        f\"(alpha={alpha}, min_size={min_size}).\"\n    )\n\ndef feature_cluster_partition(X, y, n_clients, n_clusters, seed):\n    km = MiniBatchKMeans(n_clusters=n_clusters, random_state=seed, batch_size=256, n_init=10)\n    cluster_id = km.fit_predict(X)\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    parts = [[] for _ in range(n_clients)]\n    for c in range(n_clusters):\n        idx = rng.permutation(np.where(cluster_id == c)[0])\n        if len(idx) == 0:\n            continue\n        props = rng.dirichlet(np.ones(n_clients) * 0.35)\n        cuts = (np.cumsum(props) * len(idx)).astype(int)[:-1]\n        for k, s in enumerate(np.split(idx, cuts)):\n            parts[k].extend(s.tolist())\n    for k in range(n_clients):\n        if len(parts[k]) == 0:\n            donor = int(np.argmax([len(z) for z in parts]))\n            parts[k].append(parts[donor].pop())\n    return [np.array(sorted(z), dtype=int) for z in parts], cluster_id\n\ndef client_summary(parts, y, cluster_id=None):\n    rows=[]\n    global_rate=float(np.mean(y))\n    for k, idx in enumerate(parts):\n        row={\"client\":k, \"n\":len(idx),\n             \"label1_rate\":float(np.mean(y[idx])),\n             \"abs_label_shift\":abs(float(np.mean(y[idx]))-global_rate)}\n        if cluster_id is not None:\n            vals, counts=np.unique(cluster_id[idx], return_counts=True)\n            row[\"n_feature_clusters\"]=len(vals)\n            row[\"dominant_cluster_share\"]=float(counts.max()/counts.sum())\n        rows.append(row)\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\niid_parts = balanced_iid_partition(y_train, N_CLIENTS, SEED)\ndir_parts = dirichlet_label_partition(y_train, N_CLIENTS, 0.5, SEED)\ncluster_parts, cluster_ids = feature_cluster_partition(\n    X_train, y_train, N_CLIENTS, N_FEATURE_CLUSTERS, SEED\n)\n\nprint(\"IID\"); display(client_summary(iid_parts, y_train))\nprint(\"Dirichlet alpha=0.5\"); display(client_summary(dir_parts, y_train))\nprint(\"Cluster-skew\"); display(client_summary(cluster_parts, y_train, cluster_ids))\n# ============================================\n# 7A. Inspect heterogeneity at different alpha\n# ============================================\n\nprint(\"========== IID ==========\")\n\niid_parts = balanced_iid_partition(\n    y_train,\n    N_CLIENTS,\n    SEED\n)\n\ndisplay(\n    client_summary(\n        iid_parts,\n        y_train\n    )\n)\n\nfor alpha in CFG[\"alphas\"]:\n\n    print(\n        f\"\\n========== Dirichlet alpha={alpha} ==========\"\n    )\n\n    parts = dirichlet_label_partition(\n        y_train,\n        N_CLIENTS,\n        alpha=alpha,\n        seed=SEED,\n        min_size=100\n    )\n\n    summary = client_summary(\n        parts,\n        y_train\n    )\n\n    display(summary)\n","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-05T15:00:49.002243Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-05T15:00:49.002751Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-05T15:00:49.243497Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-05T15:00:49.002727Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-05T15:00:49.242735Z"},"trusted":true},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"IID\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"   client    n  label1_rate  abs_label_shift\n0       0  999      0.48048              0.0\n1       1  999      0.48048              0.0\n2       2  999      0.48048              0.0\n3       3  999      0.48048              0.0\n4       4  999      0.48048              0.0","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n