w-level\",\n  \"subject_ids_available\": false,\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"Clients are simulated partitions, not identified real students.\",\n    \"CAFAD validation confidence is not included in the formal DP comparison.\",\n    \"Feature-cluster skew is controlled heterogeneity, not claimed to reproduce real device populations.\"\n  ]\n}\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":27},{"id":"a674b7d4","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n# Final research protocol\n\nRun in this order:\n\n1. Dataset audit\n2. Benchmark-validity / feature-dependence audit\n3. Centralized baselines\n4. FL pilot\n5. Heterogeneity sweep\n6. Client unreliability sweep\n7. DP sweep\n8. FGSM\n9. Paired statistics + BH correction\n10. Figures/tables + saved CSVs\n\nThe paper should lead with the empirical fact that the released V3 feature representation already contains substantial information about the released operational attention label. The FL contribution then becomes a **controlled benchmark of privacy, heterogeneity and client unreliability**, rather than a claim that a new aggregator is universally superior.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"1e79d6d0-fc93-4977-9943-b38a4c5c58b7","cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n# 19. Next-step analysis and final experiments\n\nThe previous notebook contains the clean 20-seed FL sweep and several analysis cells, but it does not yet contain all of the follow-up experiments needed for the final paper.\n\nThis section adds the missing pieces:\n\n1. diagnose Median/TrimmedMean collapse and inspect update norms;\n2. run a blocked train/test sensitivity analysis;\n3. validate the full-schedule DP mechanism on a small pilot;\n4. optionally launch the full 20-seed DP privacy–utility grid;\n5. optionally run the final 20-seed FGSM evaluation;\n6. export publication-ready figures and manuscript tables.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"1b5480ef-af9b-4a6a-8eb6-e860fcd01001","cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ============================================================\n# 19A. Median / TrimmedMean failure-mode diagnosis\n# ============================================================\n\nfrom sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix\n\ndef prediction_diagnostics_from_state(state, X, y):\n    model = MLP(X.shape[1])\n    load_state_dict_cpu(model, state)\n    model.eval()\n\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        logits = model(torch.tensor(X, dtype=torch.float32))\n        pred = logits.argmax(dim=1).cpu().numpy()\n\n    cm = confusion_matrix(y, pred, labels=[0, 1])\n\n    return {\n        \"accuracy\": accuracy_score(y, pred),\n        \"balanced_accuracy\": balanced_accuracy_score(y, pred),\n        \"f1\": f1_score(y, pred, zero_division=0),\n        \"precision\": precision_score(y, pred, zero_division=0),\n        \"recall\": recall_score(y, pred, zero_division=0),\n        \"mcc\": matthews_corrcoef(y, pred),\n        \"pred_class0_rate\": float(np.mean(pred == 0)),\n        \"pred_class1_rate\": float(np.mean(pred == 1)),\n        \"cm_00\": int(cm[0, 0]),\n        \"cm_01\": int(cm[0, 1]),\n        \"cm_10\": int(cm[1, 0]),\n        \"cm_11\": int(cm[1, 1]),\n    }\n\n# Helper for update-norm diagnostics\ndef flatten_state_delta(state_a, state_b):\n    if set(state_a.keys()) != set(state_b.keys()):\n        raise ValueError(\"State dictionaries have different parameter keys.\")\n\n    return torch.cat([\n        (state_a[k].detach().float() - state_b[k].detach().float()).reshape(-1)\n        for k in state_a.keys()\n    ])\n\ndef run_federated_diagnostic(\n    X, y, X_eval, y_eval, parts, method, seed,\n    rounds, local_epochs, batch_size\n):\n    seed_everything(seed)\n    global_state = clone_state_dict(MLP(X.shape[1]))\n    round_rows = []\n\n    for rnd in range(rounds):\n        local_states, val_accs, ns = train_clients_once(\n            global_state, parts, X, y,\n            seed=seed + rnd * 1000,\n            method=method,\n            epochs=local_epochs,\n            batch_size=batch_size,\n        )\n\n        # Norm of each local update relative to the current global model.\n        local_update_norms = [\n            float(torch.linalg.vector_norm(\n                flatten_state_delta(st, global_state)\n            ))\n            for st in local_states\n        ]\n\n        global_before = global_state\n        global_state, weights, mask = aggregate(\n            method, local_states, ns, val_accs\n        )\n\n        global_update_norm = float(torch.linalg.vector_norm(\n            flatten_state_delta(global_state, global_before)\n        ))\n\n        metrics = evaluate_state(global_state, X_eval, y_eval)\n\n        row = {\n            \"round\": rnd + 1,\n            \"method\": method,\n            \"seed\": seed,\n            \"mean_client_update_norm\": float(np.mean(local_update_norms)),\n            \"max_client_update_norm\": float(np.max(local_update_norms)),\n            \"global_update_norm\": global_update_norm,\n            \"min_client_val_acc\": float(np.min(val_accs)),\n            \"max_client_val_acc\": float(np.max(val_accs)),\n            \"std_client_val_acc\": float(np.std(val_accs)),\n            \"masked_clients\": (\n                int((~mask).sum()) if mask is not None else 0\n            ),\n            **metrics\n        }\n\n        for k, v in enumerate(val_accs):\n            row[f\"client{k}_val_acc\"] = float(v)\n        for k, v in enumerate(local_update_norms):\n            row[f\"client{k}_update_norm\"] = float(v)\n\n        round_rows.append(row)\n\n    final_diag = prediction_diagnostics_from_state(\n        global_state, X_eval, y_eval\n    )\n\n    return pd.DataFrame(round_rows), final_diag, global_state\n\n# Identify worst clean runs for Median and TrimmedMean.\nworst_cases = (\n    clean_results[\n        (clean_results[\"condition\"] == \"Dirichlet\")\n        & (clean_results[\"alpha\"].isin([0.5, 0.1]))\n        & (clean_results[\"method\"].isin([\"Median\", \"TrimmedMean\"]))\n    ]\n    .nsmallest(6, \"accuracy\")\n    [[\"condition\", \"alpha\", \"method\", \"seed\", \"accuracy\", \"f1\"]]\n    .reset_index(drop=True)\n)\n\ndisplay(worst_cases)\n\ndiagnostic_history = []\ndiagnostic_final = []\n\nfor _, r in worst_cases.iterrows():\n    alpha = float(r[\"alpha\"])\n    seed = int(r[\"seed\"])\n    target_method = r[\"method\"]\n\n    parts = dirichlet_label_partition(\n        y_train, N_CLIENTS, alpha=alpha, seed=seed, min_size=100\n    )\n\n    for method in [\"FedAvg\", target_method, \"CAFAD\"]:\n        hist, final_diag, _ = run_federated_diagnostic(\n            X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test,\n            parts, method, seed,\n            CFG[\"fl_rounds\"],\n            CFG[\"local_epochs\"],\n            CFG[\"batch_size\"]\n        )\n\n        hist[\"alpha\"] = alpha\n        hist[\"target_failure_method\"] = target_method\n        diagnostic_history.append(hist)\n\n        diagnostic_final.append({\n            \"alpha\": alpha,\n            \"seed\": seed,\n            \"target_failure_method\": target_method,\n            \"method\": method,\n            **final_diag\n        })\n\ndiagnostic_history = pd.concat(\n    diagnostic_history, ignore_index=True\n)\ndiagnostic_final = pd.DataFrame(diagnostic_final)\n\ndisplay(\n    diagnostic_final.sort_values(\n        [\"alpha\", \"seed\", \"target_failure_method\", \"method\"]\n    )\n)\n\ndiagnostic_history.to_csv(\n    RESULTS_DIR / \"aggregation_failure_dynamics_v3.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\ndiagnostic_final.to_csv(\n    RESULTS_DIR / \"aggregation_failure_final_metrics_v3.csv\",\n    index=False\n)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-05T17:33:51.782048Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-05T17:33:51.782468Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-05T17:35:54.760444Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-05T17:33:51.78244Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-05T17:35:54.759523Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"   condition  alpha       method  seed  accuracy        f1\n0 